    howItProtectsYou: 'You control the outcome. If you do it yourself, it will be done right. You avoid the disappointment of relying on others. You have a clear role and purpose: "the one who handles things." Staying constantly busy also allows you to avoid your own feelings.',
    howItHurtsYouNow: 'You may eventually reach a point where concentration, patience, motivation, or ordinary functioning becomes harder to sustain. The guilt about not doing enough never stops. By refusing help, correcting other people\'s methods, or taking tasks back, you keep reinforcing the belief that everything depends on you. Your relationships become unbalanced, and other people may stop participating because there is no room to contribute. Some people with this pattern also notice exhaustion, tension, or sleep difficulties during prolonged periods of high demand. These experiences are signals to explore, not proof that overwork caused a medical condition.',
